Version 0.14.2
  o anovahv() uses the supplied observations consistently for fitting and
    summaries, and reports Welch F, degrees of freedom and p without rounding
    the stored result.
  o t.testhv() and anovahv() identify the selected analysis and handle groups
    too small for Welch. One-sample and paired tests avoid duplicate fits.
  o corrected binomial log probabilities, discrete moments and the scaling of
    histc() overlays. Probability plots now respect multi-panel layouts.
  o daria() and dariat() calculate upper tails directly. These functions and
    dbinoms() print small positive probabilities as "< 0.0001" and retain
    their numeric value for calculations.
  o dfcalc() and spooled() validate summary inputs and use scaled arithmetic.
  o multiple improvements to function anovahv()
  o new argument "numsum" to function anovahv()
  o fixes histogram height in function histc()

Version 0.13
  o function t.testAB() renamed to t.testhv()
  o function anovaFK() renamed to anovahv() where "hv" stands for
    "homogeneity of variance" testing.
  o function t.testhv() is now generic, detecting declared categorical
    variables, formulas and even Pair() class extensions.

Version 0.12
  o updated package description
  o plots now restore the original graphical parameters
  o homogeneity of variances tests report only their p-value.

Version 0.11
  o new function histc() to fraw a histogram with an added distribution
    density curve
  o t.testhv() and anovahv() have dedicated print methods
  o argument "new" from function dbinoms() is now FALSE by default
  o new argument "zoom" for function dbinoms(); if TRUE, the drawing only zooms
    on the values with a positive probability
  o new function hclr() pentru a genera culori din gama HCL (Hue Chroma Luminance)
  o function t.testhv() now also accepts a formula in the first argument
  o new function anovahv() using the Fligner-Killeen test to verify the
    homogeneity of variance assumption
  o new function dfcalc() to calculate degrees of freedom
  o new function t.testhv() using the Ansari-Bradley test to verify the
    homogeneity of variance assumption
  o new function spooled() to calculate the pooled variance

Version 0.1
  o initial version
